# Lockstep releases

ALL `@shamar/*` packages in `packages/*/package.json` ship the **same version**. Never cut a release that bumps only `@shamar/adonis` (or any single package).

## Packages (keep in sync)

`@shamar/core`, `@shamar/cherubim`, `@shamar/mongoose`, `@shamar/rest`, `@shamar/lucid`, `@shamar/wire`, `@shamar/adonis`

## Required when releasing

1. Bump **every** `packages/*/package.json` `version` to the same semver (e.g. `1.0.17`).
2. Publish **all** `@shamar/*` together (CI Publish workflow or equivalent) — do not publish only `@shamar/adonis`.
3. Update changelog / release notes for the monorepo release, not a single package.

## Forbidden

- Releasing only `@shamar/adonis` while siblings stay on an older version.
- Mixed versions across packages (e.g. adonis `1.0.17` + core `1.0.16`).
- Host apps resolving a mix of `@shamar/*` versions after a release.

## Example

```json
// ❌ BAD — only adonis bumped
"@shamar/adonis": "1.0.17"
"@shamar/core": "1.0.16"

// ✅ GOOD — lockstep
"@shamar/adonis": "1.0.17"
"@shamar/core": "1.0.17"
"@shamar/cherubim": "1.0.17"
"@shamar/mongoose": "1.0.17"
"@shamar/rest": "1.0.17"
"@shamar/lucid": "1.0.17"
"@shamar/wire": "1.0.17"
```

Hosts (e.g. class-attendance) must consume the same caret range for every direct `@shamar/*` dep after the release is on npm.
